{
  "text": "Welcome to the All-In Podcast. Let us look at the liquidity contraction hitting commercial real estate and tech startups. The era of zero interest rate policy enabled immense capital misallocation. Now that the cost of capital is five percent, every unprofitable balance sheet is breaking. Companies must show genuine free cash flow or face harsh down-rounds. The capital expenditure battle in artificial intelligence is unprecedented. Hyperscalers are investing tens of billions into datacenters and custom silicon. Whoever owns the compute infrastructure dictates the software margins of the next decade.",
